    ('35645', 0, $$Letter 's' builds words. Letter 's' makes more.$$),
    ('35645', 1, $$You can add an 's' to a word to have more. Adding 's' makes more things.$$),
    ('35645', 2, $$Adding 's' to a word forms a plural. Removing 's' from a word forms a singular.$$),
    ('35645', 3, $$Even though letter 's' builds words there are some words that change the rules.$$),
    ('35645', 4, $$If a word ends in ch, sh, s, ss, x or z then use 'es. '$$),
